* Ampeg SVT (1972, 6550 version) preamp, drawing 591719, split in four solvers (amp.json "stages", docs/PLAN_CPU.md). The whole circuit is
* preamp_full.net: the reference the split is checked against (sas_split_check). The stages:
*   preamp.net  channel 1's first tube, V1A, up to its plate p1 (the V1b follower that reads it is in stage 3);
*   stage2.net  channel 2 up to V2B's plate p2b, with the stack as its load;
*   stage3.net  channel 1 from V1b on: SW1, volume 1, V3A, stack 1, V3B, V4A (V3B's plate drives V4A's grid, which conducts, so they stay together);
*   stage4.net  the V4b follower, the mid-range network, V5 and the master, with channel 2's stack (no tube: it is only linear).
* Both channels take the guitar, so stages 1 and 2 repeat its source and pickup network. The cuts are at p1 and p4a, which only feed a follower (the
* follower reads them and loads nothing: an exact cut), and at p2b, whose load (the stack) is repeated in stage 2 and real in stage 4.
* The supply network (R47/C23 and RDEC/CDEC) is repeated in each stage with the resistors scaled by (total current / this stage's current) and the
* capacitors by the inverse: the same DC drop and time constants as when they shared it. What is lost is the interaction through the shared rail.
*
* This file: stage 1.

.nodes x rb rd gin in pkb1 pkb2 pkk1 pkk2 pkk4 jb1 jn1 g1 p1 k1

V VRAIL x 684.3 430
R R47 x rb 56.115k
C C23 rb 0 5.845u
R RDEC rb rd 28.641k
C CDEC rd 0 6.564u

I VIN gin 1
R RSRC gin in 7k
* The guitar behind its source impedance (see the other amps for the pickup model).
R RPU1 gin pkb1 1e12
.xfmr LPU1 L=2.5
  W pkb1 in 1 pu
.end
R RPU2 gin pkb2 1e12
.xfmr LPU2 L=5
  W pkb2 in 1 pu
.end
C CPU gin in 110p
R RPL gin in 1e12
R SWK1 in pkk1 1e12
C CCAB1 pkk1 0 200p
R SWK2 in pkk2 1e12
C CCAB2 pkk2 0 400p
R SWK4 in pkk4 1e12
C CCAB4 pkk4 0 800p

R SW_N1 in jn1 1
R SW_B1 in jb1 1e12
R R2 jn1 g1 47k
R R1 jb1 g1 100k
C C1 jb1 g1 4n7
R R4 g1 0 5.6M

T V1A g1 p1 k1 12AX7
R R3 rd p1 220k
R R5 k1 0 3k3
